  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a strong multimodal baseline and reduce uncertainty about the most impactful design choices. config_008 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer, weighted) tests the core hypothesis that combining RNA and image features with multiprofile transformer aggregation yields strong accuracy. It uses pca_n2000 (moderate-cost, 2000-dim linear representation) and resnet50 (solid but cheaper than ViT-L) to keep cost manageable while the transformer aggregation is the key expressive component being validated. If this performs well, it justifies investing in more expensive encoders (scgpt, ViT-L) in later experiments; if it underperforms, it signals that simpler aggregation or different encoders may suffice. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high — transformer aggregation and multiprofile processing add overhead, but avoiding ViT-L and scgpt keeps it well below the most expensive configurations (e.g., config_041/035)."
}

